rm-limited Bill Lee is stepping aside, and the state's strong Republican lean shapes everything. Senator Marsha Blackburn enters as the heavy favorite, bringing statewide name recognition and a fundraising base, while Democrat Jerri Green is a little-known challenger trying to close the gap. Polls since spring show Green stuck in the low-to-mid 30s, trailing by margins that range from nine to twenty-one points, with the most recent survey putting the gap at nine.\n\nRaters across the spectrum call the race solid or safe Republican, and prediction markets price Green's chances at about six percent. A crowded field of more than a dozen independents, including David Hatley and Lauren Pinkston, has drawn attention and agreed to debates Blackburn skipped, but history suggests scattered independents rarely decide statewide races here. The main question is the final margin, not the winner.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0257, "margin": -11.12}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0463, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0186, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0193, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0323, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0336, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0245, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.009, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0321, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0183, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0272, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0281, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0357, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0171, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0167, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0175, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0098, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0123, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0157, "margi